1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:04,240
Shouldn't you be swamped by the project?

3
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:06,200
How do you have time to come back
and space out here?

4
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,639
I wasn't spacing out. I was thinking.

5
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:13,200
I'm just organizing some materials.

6
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,280
Celestial doesn't have a place
for me to work,

7
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,680
so I came back to the office.

8
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,600
- Looks like what they're saying is true.
- What's true?

9
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,680
You and Yang Rui
made a huge fool of yourselves

10
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,960
in front of the Celestial client.

11
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:28,840
You threw away all the goodwill

12
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,160
we built with the client
after they accepted the overall plan.

13
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,960
Now they won't even give you
a workstation.

14
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:34,320
Don't talk nonsense!

15
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,000
Who told you that?
Don't go spreading that around.

16
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,160
I'm just giving you a heads-up.

17
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:52,440
You've been in the spotlight too much.

18
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,440
A lot of people at the company
are waiting to see you fall.

19
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:00,920
Just now at the meeting,
someone told Sha Sha you're too arrogant.

20
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:04,400
They said you argued with Tianna
in front of the client at Celestial.

21
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,200
I didn't argue with her.

22
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,000
I was just bickering with her.

23
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:10,040
I know. But other people don't.

24
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,800
So I'm just reminding you.

25
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:12,920
One, tone it down.

26
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,640
Two, if something
goes wrong with Yang Rui,

27
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:16,680
don't take the fall for him.

28
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,800
He doesn't listen to me at all.

29
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,280
And he's my boyfriend.

30
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,240
I can't go complain about him to Ma Ke.

31
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:25,720
That's it then.

32
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:38,840
<i>You believe gossip like that?</i>

33
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,440
<i>That's not like you.</i>

34
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,920
<i>If you feel uncomfortable</i>
<i>being at the office alone,</i>

35
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,040
<i>I'll come back</i>
<i>to keep you company next Monday.</i>

36
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,360
I don't need you to keep me company.

37
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:49,240
I want to draft a new proposal
for their IT Department,

38
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:51,600
<i>so they can see</i>
<i>our sincerity and capability.</i>

39
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,360
<i>At least so they don't think</i>
<i>Maxmise is all talk and no action.</i>

40
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,040
Ma Ke said to put it on hold.

41
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,320
<i>He'll handle it.</i>

42
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,960
<i>Can you not go off on your own like this?</i>

43
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,800
Sorry. I sounded harsh just now.

44
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,840
<i>Don't take it to heart.</i>

45
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,640
<i>I just think you shouldn't</i>
<i>keep butting heads with Ma Ke.</i>

46
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:09,040
- <i>After all, last time--</i>
- I know.

47
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:10,800
<i>Alright.</i>

48
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:12,680
<i>Celestial is having a team-building event</i>
<i>this weekend, isn't it?</i>

49
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:14,640
<i>We can go out together on our day off.</i>

50
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:15,560
<i>How about Huanying World?</i>

51
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,880
Sure. We'll figure it out later.

52
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,040
YE XINZHI

53
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,880
<i>Tonight at 8:30. J Center, 120th Floor.</i>

54
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,960
<i>I'm meeting with the MD</i>
<i>of Morse Investment Bank</i>

55
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,760
<i>to broker a deal for Tianhe Air.</i>

56
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,320
<i>Can you come be my temporary secretary?</i>

57
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,280
Your first time here?

58
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,360
Yeah.

59
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:17,200
So I just took a bunch of photos
and posted them on Moments.

60
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:19,120
Once you've been here a few dozen times,

61
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,720
you'll only complain
about how long the elevator takes.

62
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,360
But even then,

63
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:29,440
face-to-face time
with Morse's MD is still rare.

64
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:37,320
We're here to discuss
the Tianhe plan today.

65
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:41,040
Isn't your outfit a bit too casual?

66
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,040
I've known him for a long time.

67
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:45,600
Dressing too formally
actually feels a bit odd.

68
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,320
But what you're wearing is just right.

69
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,240
Relax.

70
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:53,840
Relax, and you'll be at your best.

71
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,160
Relax.

72
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,680
Don't forget how you bragged to Tianna.

73
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:05,480
How come the moment you meet,
you're the only one freaking out?

74
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:07,560
Thank you for the postcard you sent me.

75
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:10,200
The small building in the picture
is exactly the same as I remember.

76
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:12,080
- Happy?
- Yeah.

77
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,320
Then I'm even happier.

78
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,240
Foul. That's just foul.

79
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,320
What would you two like to drink?

80
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,480
- Jiwa.
- Jiwa, thanks.

81
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,480
You two are so in sync.

82
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:37,720
- I'll have an Americano.
- Sure, sir.

83
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,000
- Mr. Deng.
- Mr. Ye.

84
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,040
Let me introduce you.

85
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,360
This is my assistant, Chi.

86
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,440
- Hello. I'm Xu Chi.
- Hello.

87
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,440
If this deal goes through,
I really have to thank you.

88
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,400
Why be so formal with me?

89
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:12,040
I happen to be consulting for Tianhe.

90
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,800
I know they have investment needs,

91
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,040
and I know you've got plenty of capital.

92
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,280
It's just a small favor.

93
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,920
Tianhe really hit the jackpot
hiring you as consultants.

94
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:25,280
Miss Xu, please organize
the meeting minutes when you get back.

95
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,360
Once I receive them tomorrow,
I'll reach out to them right away.

96
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,120
Already sent to your email.

97
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,160
I trained her personally.

98
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,560
Very fast.

99
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:36,120
And her accuracy is just as good.

100
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,160
I'm not worried about that.

101
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,280
Because just now,

102
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,000
many of Miss Xu's points
really impressed me.

103
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,440
Miss Xu, would you consider
joining my company?

104
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,760
I've long heard that the chef
at Morse's Beijing headquarters

105
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:54,200
elite staff restaurant
was hired from a top five-star hotel.

106
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:57,160
If you'd like to take me along
for a good meal,

107
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,080
I can leave right now.

108
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,640
Let's go.

109
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:02,360
Deng. Poaching in front of me, huh?

110
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:05,840
Joking aside.

111
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:08,920
You know, I really admire you guys.

112
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,040
No matter what industry you consult for,

113
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,600
you're always so professional.

114
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:15,160
Consultants are supposed to know
the industry better than the clients.

115
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,840
You can't just pull a random case
from the files and churn out a proposal.

116
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:21,360
Fooling the client and fooling yourself?

117
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,680
That's not how I do things.

118
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,280
<i>That's what makes you impressive.</i>

119
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,800
<i>Maxmise isn't magic.</i>

120
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,880
How could we possibly know
every company's technical details?

121
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:31,120
Just showing them a tiny bit
is more than enough.

122
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,280
Let's wish us success.

123
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,559
Success.

124
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:57,880
You're not still thinking
about Celestial's IT Department, are you?

125
00:09:00,160 --> 00:09:01,120
No.

126
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:02,760
I… I was moved by the movie.

127
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:06,480
This is a comedy.

128
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,280
Laughing through tears
is what makes it really touching.

129
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,480
I'm going to the restroom.

130
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,040
So embarrassing.

131
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:48,440
Xu Chi.

132
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:53,080
Lin? What a coincidence.
Are you here to see a movie too?

133
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:54,600
I saw you earlier.

134
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,960
I wanted to thank you
for helping me find that agent.

135
00:09:57,040 --> 00:09:59,880
I've finished moving,
and the divorce is done.

136
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,240
I feel totally free.

137
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,560
So I wanted to catch a few movies
before my leave ends, just to relax.

138
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,840
That's great.

139
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:09,560
I think I saw you
come in with Yang Rui earlier.

140
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,400
Yeah.

141
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,560
We haven't been together long.

142
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:18,400
I thought I was seeing things.

143
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,160
How did you end up with Yang Rui?

144
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,200
Is there something wrong with him?

145
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,200
No, that's not what I meant.

146
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,760
He joined the company two years after me,

147
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,360
but he's a good consultant.

148
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,680
He's a decent guy with a good personality.

149
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:32,560
Then why…?

150
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:36,640
I just thought you and Ye Xinzhi
were pretty close before.

151
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,680
I assumed you two…

152
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:40,760
No, no. You've got it wrong.

153
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,640
My family and he are friends.

154
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:52,640
Actually, years ago,
Richard was my mentor.

155
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:55,680
He really is charming.

156
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:59,600
I even had a little crush on him once.

157
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:03,720
But looking back now,
it was probably just admiration.

158
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,800
I interned under him at Boen
for over half a year,

159
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:08,920
so I know him very well.

160
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,560
He's very cautious.

161
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:11,960
So cautious that he'd never

162
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,200
go to dinner alone
with a female colleague.

163
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:16,800
So that night when I saw him drunk
and leaning on you,

164
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,640
I got really angry.

165
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,040
But that proved

166
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:23,000
he'd already let you
into his inner circle.

167
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,880
And I could tell
you have feelings for him.

168
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:30,680
- Lin, I…
- You don't have to rush to deny it.

169
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:35,120
The fact that I can say all this openly
shows I've long since let it go.

170
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,680
His type is what young girls fall for.

171
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:40,600
I'm way past liking that type now.

172
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,080
You should get going.

173
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:46,000
See you at the office.

174
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:54,880
FISH SPINNERS

175
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:11,240
Look at that.

176
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:22,200
BEIJING HAPPY VALLEY

177
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:38,480
LONG TIME NO SIP, TIPSY BAR

178
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,600
- Let's buy some water.
- Sure.

179
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,000
Here.

180
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,880
This water is pretty expensive, isn't it?

181
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,680
I grabbed the wrong one.

182
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:49,600
Which one do you want?

183
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:53,080
Hello. Two bottles of this, please.

184
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:54,480
- That's 20 total.
- Okay.

185
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,160
- Let me.
- I'll pay.

186
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,080
Let me.

187
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:01,360
Alright. Thanks.

188
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,120
Thank you.

189
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:23,720
<i>Lin.</i>

190
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,680
Back then,

191
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:30,040
how did you control your feelings for him?

192
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:33,920
I left Boen and joined Maxmise.

193
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,280
Yang Rui is my "Maxmise".

194
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,360
I get it.

195
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,920
I won't try to talk you out of it.

196
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,280
After all, you know only

197
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:49,320
if a relationship is worth it
once you've been in it.

198
00:13:49,920 --> 00:13:52,400
But as someone who's been divorced,
let me share one piece of experience.

199
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,720
If you're with someone you like,

200
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:55,880
no matter how busy or tired you are,

201
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,520
you'll be happy.

202
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:01,560
But if you're with someone
you don't like that much,

203
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:04,360
you won't last long before you get tired.

204
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:07,440
Yang Rui.

205
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,880
- I--
- Let's break up.

206
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:15,640
Actually, I've been wanting
to say this to you.

207
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,520
I just didn't know how.

208
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:21,480
Honestly, when we first got together,
I was really happy.

209
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:25,800
But over time, I realized
there was no real spark between us.

210
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:29,000
We're just not meant to be together.

211
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:33,720
Because we're interested
in different things.

212
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:37,040
And every time we go on a date,
we're not on the same page.

213
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:40,680
We were always just trying it out anyway.

214
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:43,240
But I figured if one day

215
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:45,400
you dumped me first,
that'd be pretty embarrassing.

216
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:47,680
So I might as well beat you to it.

217
00:14:51,840 --> 00:14:54,880
Where are your manners?
Whatever happened to "ladies first"?

218
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,800
We're both corporate drones.
Let's not bother with gender.

219
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,640
- We're still good colleagues.
- Of course.

220
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,200
And friends.

221
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:07,640
<i>Good breakup.</i>

222
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:10,240
You and Yang Rui
never had any chemistry anyway.

223
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,960
And you getting publicly criticized

224
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:15,200
by Mr. Sun from Celestial's IT Department
was all thanks to him.

225
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:19,560
We talked it over. Since we broke up,

226
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:21,280
staying in the same project team
would be awkward,

227
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,120
so I want to apply
for a transfer to another team.

228
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,720
Come to our team.

229
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:27,400
Let's really join forces
and do something big together.

230
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,480
Sure.

231
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:30,720
I think there's too much dust

232
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:33,160
in your router, so it's overheating,
and the WiFi keeps dropping.

233
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:34,680
Let me wipe it down. That should fix it.

234
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,480
Now

235
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:40,680
you've broken up with Yang Rui.

236
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:41,880
You're single again.

237
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:43,920
How are you moving things
forward with Ye Xinzhi?

238
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:46,160
Move what forward?

239
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,840
Just go back to how things were.

240
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,640
Once you've had the best,
nobody else compares.

241
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:51,880
Since I like him,

242
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:54,280
I won't force myself
to be with someone else.

243
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,240
I'm just not good enough
for him right now.

244
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:57,920
Then I'll work for it.

245
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,000
I'll learn from him
while keeping things flirtatious.

246
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,440
Maybe one day I'll deserve him.

247
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:04,680
Then I'll have both career and love.

248
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,760
"Once you've had the best,
nobody else compares"?

249
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,040
Have you even had him?

250
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:13,160
Have you even been through anything?

251
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:14,480
That's just a secret crush.

252
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:16,040
Don't flatter yourself.

253
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:20,680
Let me tell you,

254
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,320
after we met with Mr. Deng
from Morse that day,

255
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:24,960
Ye Xinzhi drove me back to the hotel.
He sat in the back seat with me.

256
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:28,760
I have a feeling if he knew I broke up,
he'd be pretty happy.

257
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,080
What are you laughing at?

258
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:34,040
The two of you are worlds apart in status.

259
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,520
He's way up there.

260
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:37,240
Should he sit in the front
instead of the back?

261
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:40,960
Besides, if some young girl were putting
herself on a silver platter for me,

262
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:42,160
I'd be loving it too.

263
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:44,640
I'm not fixing your router.

264
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:46,200
Just leave it. Let the WiFi stay broken.

265
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,400
- I'm done.
- Can't handle…

266
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:49,960
Can't handle facing reality?

267
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:55,480
Anyway, he's not the kind
of textbook scumbag you described.

268
00:16:56,000 --> 00:17:01,520
He hasn't made a move
because he has feelings for me,

269
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:02,680
but he's just not in love with me yet.

270
00:17:02,760 --> 00:17:03,920
But just you wait.

271
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,200
One day,

272
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:08,480
I'll become a woman he can't resist.

273
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,599
How exactly "can't resist" are we talking?

274
00:17:24,359 --> 00:17:28,280
Do you really want to know?

275
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,520
Gross.

276
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,560
You sure you don't want to know?

277
00:17:35,480 --> 00:17:36,960
I'm just wondering…

278
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:39,520
What if you don't become that woman?

279
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:43,000
And even if you do,
what if he won't commit to you?

280
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,000
Don't blame me for raining on your parade.

281
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:50,080
I looked it up. He's been divorced.

282
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:52,920
He's been divorced!

283
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,800
I know. I know. I looked it up too.

284
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:57,360
Miss Bu, why are you such a pessimist?

285
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:59,720
First of all, nothing's
even started between us yet.

286
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,160
Why think about the ending?

287
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:02,960
Second, in love,

288
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:06,400
the dopamine only lasts
about three months on average.

289
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:08,400
Maybe by then I'll be the one
who gets bored first.

290
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:11,960
Then he's only good
for what I can learn from him.

291
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:15,000
Once I've squeezed him dry,
it'll be my turn to…

292
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,440
And how exactly are you going
to squeeze him dry?

293
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,200
Bu Tianna.

294
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:30,960
- Will you cut it out?
- Will you…

295
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:32,000
What are you doing?

296
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:32,920
Is this how you squeeze him?

297
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,560
Bu Tianna, you… I'm going to hit you.

298
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:35,600
Is this the squeeze?

299
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:36,840
I…

300
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:39,200
Help! Do you still want me
to fix your router or not?

301
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,880
What are you doing?

302
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:42,560
So you can make dirty jokes about me,
but I can't do that to you?

303
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:44,760
You're no fun.

304
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,400
Okay, fine.

305
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:47,720
Then hire a repair guy to fix it.

306
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:48,640
Don't ask me to do it.

307
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,440
- Because you don't charge.
- Are you short on money?

308
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:51,720
Yeah.

309
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:55,840
I just don't want strange men in my place.

310
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:59,760
And most people
who fix this stuff are men.

311
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:02,840
But Zhao Heng
came by the other day, didn't he?

312
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:06,400
Is he not a stranger, or not a man?

313
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,000
‪He…

314
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:38,960
Who is it? Who's there?

315
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:40,880
Who is it?

316
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:44,480
- It's me.
- What are you doing here?

317
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:47,120
Didn't your WiFi go down?
And your computer too?

318
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,320
Last time, I noticed

319
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,240
the property management
gave you an old router.

320
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:51,480
The signal's bad.

321
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:52,400
This one's better.

322
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,680
Did I ask you about the router?

323
00:19:53,760 --> 00:19:57,240
I asked why you came to my place
without my permission.

324
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:58,520
Because of love.

325
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:03,320
What's wrong?

326
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,000
Who's there? Do you have someone over?

327
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,520
Speak of the devil.

328
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,880
Devil? Are you two talking about me?

329
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:12,800
Putting on a show?

330
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,480
Yeah.

331
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:16,360
Fine. I already fixed it for you.

332
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,520
I'm heading out.

333
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:20,360
I'll leave you two to it,
whether it's just talking or full action.

334
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:21,480
Either way.

335
00:20:21,560 --> 00:20:22,720
- I'm off.
- Wait.

336
00:20:23,320 --> 00:20:25,040
- I'm leaving with you.
- Where are you going?

337
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:25,880
Home.

338
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:27,840
Home?

339
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,400
You're going home,
given how bad things are with your family?

340
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:31,080
What do you mean, bad?

341
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:33,760
I left quietly last time.

342
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:34,960
I didn't burn any bridges.

343
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:39,360
And I'm not going
to just follow their script.

344
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:41,760
They're stringing me along.
I can string them along too.

345
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,560
I'll play the loving daughter

346
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:46,520
while slowly seizing control
of Siwei Group.

347
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:47,720
Besides, Bu Tianjie is just a kid.

348
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:49,760
By the time he's old enough to take over,

349
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:52,320
who knows who Siwei Group will belong to.

350
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,600
It'll belong to the Bu family.

351
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,480
- Let's go.
- Wait.

352
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:59,200
You still haven't said
how you're going to tell Ye Xinzhi

353
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:00,360
you broke up.

354
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,760
I've got an ace up my sleeve.

355
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,360
Accidental run-ins work best.

356
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,480
Why are you sitting down?

357
00:21:11,520 --> 00:21:12,800
And with your shoes on?

358
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,160
Aren't I marrying into the family?

359
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:18,320
From now on, just call me "Bu Shoes-On"!

360
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:29,520
Alright. Your license plate
is restricted today.

361
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:33,280
I promise I won't stay a minute longer
after dropping you off.

362
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:36,240
Stop doubting fate
when it brings us together, will you?

363
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,640
What fate?

364
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:42,560
Don't flatter yourself.

365
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:44,480
There is no fate between us.

366
00:21:45,440 --> 00:21:46,560
So cold-hearted.

367
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,000
Zhao Heng, listen.

368
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:53,680
Even if I used your shoulder once
when I was down, so what?

369
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,880
We are never taking this any further.

370
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:58,600
I never said
I needed us to take it further.

371
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:01,160
I actually think
we're great just like this.

372
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,600
Zhao Heng, I'm telling you this
for the very last time.

373
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:07,480
Stop wasting your time on me.

374
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:09,480
It's never going to happen between us.

375
00:22:09,560 --> 00:22:13,160
And I'll tell you this one last time too.

376
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:15,000
Relationships take two people.

377
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:17,440
It's not your decision alone to make.

378
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:20,920
How can you be so thick-skinned?

379
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:24,960
I made myself crystal clear,
and you're still clinging to me? Why?

380
00:22:25,040 --> 00:22:27,480
I don't even like you!

381
00:22:33,000 --> 00:22:35,600
I know every single trick
you scheming guys like to pull.

382
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:38,080
You're just trying to take
advantage of my vulnerability.

383
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:39,640
How would you know so well?

384
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:49,120
<i>Have you been burned</i>
<i>by a scheming guy before?</i>

385
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:56,720
You've got looks, talent,
and family background.

386
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,160
But at your age,
you have zero interest in relationships.

387
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:03,960
And you're completely on guard
whenever a man gets close.

388
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:06,280
And when you saw
Xu Chi and Ye Xinzhi getting close,

389
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:07,240
you kept warning her.

390
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:11,960
I remember you always told us
your family favors boys over girls.

391
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:13,240
But I've never heard you

392
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:15,240
mention them pressuring you
to get married.

393
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:20,320
I get it now.

394
00:23:21,560 --> 00:23:25,160
You must've been deeply hurt by a gentle,
mature, scheming guy.

395
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:28,040
Hurt so bad that even your parents
don't dare bring it up.

396
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:31,400
Hurt so bad
that you're once bitten, twice shy.

397
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:33,120
What does the down payment
on your old house have to do with me?

398
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:35,040
What right do you have
to have my jewelry appraised?

399
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:37,040
Do you know that was a birthday gift
from my dad?

400
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:42,600
Get lost.

401
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,640
And he probably got close to you

402
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:47,640
right around when you came back
from abroad and found out

403
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:49,000
you had a little brother. Am I wrong?

404
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:51,120
So you're really afraid of me
taking advantage of your vulnerability.

405
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:52,040
Pull over.

406
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:53,960
I don't have time for your stories.

407
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:56,080
- I didn't even say anything…
- Are you pulling over or not?

408
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:58,440
If you don't, I'll grab
the steering wheel right now,

409
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,360
and we'll both go down together.

410
00:24:00,520 --> 00:24:02,840
You want to die with me? That works too.

411
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:06,720
- One, two…
- How can you be so shameless?

412
00:24:06,800 --> 00:24:07,720
Didn't your mom teach you any manners?

413
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:18,840
Say whatever you want about me.

414
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,400
Just leave my parents out of this.

415
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:22,640
It must take
a special kind of toxic parents

416
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:25,440
- to raise someone as shameless as you.
- Apologize!

417
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:26,840
Or I'll never talk to you again!

418
00:24:26,920 --> 00:24:27,760
You…

419
00:24:29,080 --> 00:24:30,120
You better mean it!

420
00:24:30,840 --> 00:24:31,680
I've got plenty of simps.

421
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:33,440
One less won't matter.

422
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:50,000
Miss, you're back.

423
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:19,760
No, I'm not going!

424
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:20,880
I'm not getting that shot!

425
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:22,680
So noisy.

426
00:25:24,280 --> 00:25:26,200
- Xiaojie.
- What's all the racket?

427
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:28,880
Bad guy! Let me go!

428
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:32,560
Mrs. Bu told me to take Xiaojie
to get his vaccine before she left,

429
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:33,920
but he just won't cooperate.

430
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,440
- Xiaojie, be a good boy.
- No!

431
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:38,000
Xiaojie, it really doesn't hurt.

432
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:39,280
- Just go.
- Move.

433
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:40,520
Get up!

434
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:43,560
- Miss.
- Miss, you…

435
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:45,840
Stay right there. Don't move!

436
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,200
You two, step back.

437
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:49,560
So you don't get hurt.

438
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:03,240
- Are you going or not?
- No!

439
00:26:03,320 --> 00:26:05,400
I'm asking you one last time.
Going or not?

440
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,800
Not a chance!

441
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:12,520
Are you going or not?

442
00:26:13,160 --> 00:26:15,360
Yes. I'll go.

443
00:26:16,280 --> 00:26:17,760
There. Nice and easy.

444
00:26:46,120 --> 00:26:47,440
This is the place.

445
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:50,480
Based on his habits,

446
00:26:50,560 --> 00:26:52,400
he should come at a fixed time every week.

447
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:19,320
- Why is she here?
- No idea.

448
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:22,600
Aren't you gonna go say hi?

449
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:25,320
- Okay. Give me a sec.
- Alright.

450
00:27:43,360 --> 00:27:45,280
- What are you doing here?
- I should be asking you.

451
00:27:45,360 --> 00:27:47,040
What are you doing here?
I've always worked out here.

452
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:52,680
I've been wanting
to try some equipment lately.

453
00:27:53,320 --> 00:27:56,120
I saw on WeChat
that they offer weekend trials.

454
00:27:56,200 --> 00:27:57,440
And it's close to my place.
Thought I'd check it out.

455
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:02,520
Working hard, huh.

456
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:04,480
It's Saturday.

457
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:06,040
Not out having fun with friends?

458
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:19,280
Um…

459
00:28:21,080 --> 00:28:22,280
I broke up.

460
00:28:32,280 --> 00:28:33,760
Really?

461
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:34,920
Sorry to hear that.

462
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:38,960
So,

463
00:28:40,240 --> 00:28:42,200
I just wanted to come sweat it out today.

464
00:28:45,240 --> 00:28:46,200
Yeah.

465
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,920
Sweating it out is good.

466
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:53,160
Sweat it all out and you forget
all your troubles.

467
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,960
For you.

468
00:28:56,080 --> 00:28:58,360
I'm going boxing.

469
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:09,800
Ran off.

470
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:11,920
Go boxing?

471
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:13,640
That's it?

472
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,280
Can't look back.

473
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:33,800
And I can't leave now either.

474
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:36,800
If I leave, he'll definitely notice.

475
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:11,760
PRIVATE, DO NOT ENTER

476
00:30:24,040 --> 00:30:25,760
What is it now?

477
00:30:30,760 --> 00:30:31,720
Coming.

478
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:37,640
You tattled again?

479
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,800
Tattled about what?

480
00:30:41,360 --> 00:30:45,120
I just got home
and saw him squirming by the car,

481
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:46,200
refusing to get in.

482
00:30:46,280 --> 00:30:49,360
He said he'll only get the vaccine
if you take him.

483
00:30:50,080 --> 00:30:51,240
I'm not going.

484
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:52,280
I'm busy.

485
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:55,640
You're clearly not working right now.

486
00:30:55,720 --> 00:30:57,720
What's the big deal about
taking Xiaojie out?

487
00:30:57,800 --> 00:31:00,200
It's rare he's so attached to you.

488
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:04,120
Your dad and I both want you two
to get along.

489
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:06,320
Just go with him.

490
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:11,560
You really want me to take you?

491
00:31:12,080 --> 00:31:13,360
Can I hit him if he doesn't behave?

492
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:15,600
Of course. You're his sister.

493
00:31:16,760 --> 00:31:17,960
He's all yours.

494
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:22,960
Just get along, you two. I'm off.

495
00:31:26,680 --> 00:31:27,680
Sit.

496
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:56,360
What is wrong with you?

497
00:31:58,160 --> 00:31:59,320
Are you alright?

498
00:31:59,400 --> 00:32:01,080
I… I'm fine.

499
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:03,600
It's okay. Don't be scared.

500
00:32:03,680 --> 00:32:05,640
I… I'm not scared.

501
00:32:06,760 --> 00:32:09,040
Oh my. Scared me to death.

502
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:14,840
You really wanted me
to come with you that badly?

503
00:32:16,440 --> 00:32:17,520
Why?

504
00:32:18,560 --> 00:32:20,360
Because shots hurt.

505
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:22,120
You broke wooden boards
and didn't feel a thing.

506
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:26,240
I wanted to borrow some of your courage,

507
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:27,400
so it won't hurt as much.

508
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:42,160
Come on.

509
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:47,120
She's gone.

510
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,240
Your little girl's gone.

511
00:32:52,560 --> 00:32:54,080
She looked so down.
Aren't you gonna go after her?

512
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:55,680
No.

513
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:57,600
Let's keep training.

514
00:33:03,280 --> 00:33:05,280
Did you take some kind of power pill?
That hurt like crazy.

515
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:06,880
You're off today.

516
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:08,360
She leaves, and you take it out on me?

517
00:33:09,440 --> 00:33:10,520
Do you keep training or what?

518
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:12,400
Let's… Let's take a break.

519
00:33:12,480 --> 00:33:13,640
My hand hurts.

520
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:16,240
What did you two talk about?

521
00:33:20,360 --> 00:33:21,200
Nothing much.

522
00:33:22,120 --> 00:33:23,800
She just told me

523
00:33:25,600 --> 00:33:26,760
she broke up with her boyfriend.

524
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:30,360
Well, that's great!

525
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:31,920
That's good news.

526
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,480
She's single,

527
00:33:33,560 --> 00:33:35,400
so she'll have more time for work, right?

528
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:37,480
So that gives you an opening. Right?

529
00:33:40,560 --> 00:33:41,640
Wait, what opening?

530
00:33:42,240 --> 00:33:43,440
- Am I that kind of guy?
- Wait. What are you doing?

531
00:33:43,520 --> 00:33:47,720
- Hey, am I that kind of guy?
- What are you doing?

532
00:33:47,800 --> 00:33:49,240
W-What did I say? I…

533
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:50,800
An opening. Like,

534
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:53,720
more chances for you two
to work together. What?

535
00:33:53,800 --> 00:33:55,080
What were you thinking?

536
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:56,440
What were you thinking?

537
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:58,400
What were you thinking?
What were you thinking?

538
00:34:01,880 --> 00:34:04,480
Okay, stop. Let's get back to training.

539
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,000
- Come on.
- Yeah.

540
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:07,160
You really should work out more.

541
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:08,800
Exercise keeps you young.

542
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:12,360
That way, the age gap
between you and your little girl

543
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:13,719
won't show as much.

544
00:34:15,639 --> 00:34:17,080
Do I look that old?

545
00:34:17,600 --> 00:34:18,760
See for yourself.

546
00:34:38,560 --> 00:34:39,800
- Don't move. Stay still.
- No!

547
00:34:39,880 --> 00:34:41,480
- Stay still. Hands down.
- I don't want it!

548
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:42,880
Don't move.

549
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,400
- Stay still!
- Trust me. It won't hurt at all.

550
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,159
He's moving so much,
I can't give him the shot.

551
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:51,960
Then…

552
00:34:56,040 --> 00:34:57,000
Just pretend.

553
00:34:57,080 --> 00:34:58,040
Don't actually stick me.

554
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:11,600
Look at me. Watch closely.

555
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:30,560
See that? Doesn't hurt at all.

556
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,320
- Did you hear that?
- Yeah.

557
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:35,880
Then let's do it.

558
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:59,680
Tianna, did it hurt just now?

559
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:02,840
I'm a karate expert.

560
00:36:02,920 --> 00:36:04,040
What's a little pain?

561
00:36:04,880 --> 00:36:05,880
Here. Have some candy.

562
00:36:07,920 --> 00:36:08,920
I don't like candy.

563
00:36:09,440 --> 00:36:10,280
You take it.

564
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:13,960
Even if you're not afraid of pain,
shots still hurt.

565
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:15,520
In cartoons,

566
00:36:15,600 --> 00:36:18,400
girls feel better after eating candy.

567
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:19,840
Mom won't let me eat candy.

568
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,640
She says it'll rot my teeth.

569
00:36:21,720 --> 00:36:24,320
I worked so hard to hide this one.

570
00:36:31,320 --> 00:36:32,480
What's so great about candy?

571
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:34,680
You keep it.

572
00:37:00,520 --> 00:37:01,560
I'll take you for ice cream.

573
00:37:02,480 --> 00:37:03,520
Really?

574
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:04,920
You're not lying to me?

575
00:37:05,440 --> 00:37:07,120
Ice cream! Ice cream!

576
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:08,680
Stay still.

577
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:10,560
If you move again, I won't take you.

578
00:37:12,680 --> 00:37:15,200
I also want donuts.

579
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:17,560
And cotton candy.

580
00:37:18,280 --> 00:37:19,320
Tianna, you're my favorite.

581
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,320
My favorite!

582
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:24,960
Tianna.

583
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:28,680
Will you be the CEO for me?

584
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:31,360
I don't wanna be a CEO.

585
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:36,920
Dad always says when I grow up,
I'll be the CEO.

586
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:40,000
But I don't wanna be busy
like Dad every day.

587
00:37:40,720 --> 00:37:42,000
I just wanna play.

588
00:37:44,520 --> 00:37:45,560
Silly.

589
00:37:46,200 --> 00:37:47,400
When you grow up,
you won't think that way anymore.

590
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:12,920
What's wrong?

591
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:16,440
No luck with Ye the Legend either?

592
00:38:24,480 --> 00:38:29,960
I waited all afternoon
just to tell him I'm single now,

593
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:34,280
and he just went, "Oh, really?

594
00:38:35,080 --> 00:38:36,400
Well, I'm going boxing."

595
00:38:38,920 --> 00:38:41,280
I bet you've never met anyone
as delusional as me.

596
00:38:42,040 --> 00:38:42,960
There's another one right here.

597
00:38:43,040 --> 00:38:44,640
Come on.

598
00:38:45,760 --> 00:38:48,520
Fellow losers in love. Come on, forget it.

599
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:12,160
YE THE LEGEND

600
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:15,200
<i>I'm at a meeting by the lake tonight.</i>

601
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:16,560
<i>The moonlight is beautiful.</i>

602
00:39:16,640 --> 00:39:17,840
<i>Just wanted to send it to you.</i>

603
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:19,240
<i>Good night. Sleep well.</i>

604
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:21,040
THE MOONLIGHT IS BEAUTIFUL TONIGHT

605
00:39:21,640 --> 00:39:22,960
Scumbag.

606
00:39:23,600 --> 00:39:25,840
He ignores me,
then sends me stuff like this.

607
00:39:25,920 --> 00:39:26,760
What does he want?

608
00:39:30,960 --> 00:39:31,960
What's wrong?

609
00:39:40,800 --> 00:39:41,920
Are you okay?

610
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:44,960
Here, drink this. Tomato juice.

611
00:39:46,480 --> 00:39:48,320
I'm fine. I'm not drunk.

612
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:49,360
SONGFENG RESTAURANT

613
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:50,920
Just drink it.

614
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,520
Anyone who's drunk says they're not drunk.

615
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:53,720
It's got fructose.

616
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:55,440
It'll make your stomach feel better.

617
00:39:58,960 --> 00:40:00,040
Chi.

618
00:40:00,960 --> 00:40:03,400
How come I never noticed
how caring you are?

619
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:05,440
Oh my God.

620
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:07,560
I…

621
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:10,760
I'm taking care of the guy
who's pursuing my best friend.

622
00:40:10,840 --> 00:40:12,880
Do you think I'm not acting
like enough of a pick-me?

623
00:40:16,040 --> 00:40:17,000
What are you doing?

624
00:40:17,080 --> 00:40:19,840
Let me run something by you, Chi.

625
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:23,080
Actually, I've always thought
we'd be a good match.

626
00:40:24,080 --> 00:40:26,760
Look, you've got nothing going on.
I'm hopeless too.

627
00:40:26,840 --> 00:40:29,320
Let's just get together and piss them off.

628
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:31,400
Go away.

629
00:40:37,720 --> 00:40:39,920
Just think about it.
Hey, let's talk about it.

630
00:40:40,680 --> 00:40:43,040
Go home and sober up.

631
00:40:43,560 --> 00:40:44,400
Come on.

632
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:46,680
Go, go, go.

633
00:40:46,760 --> 00:40:47,640
Water.

634
00:40:49,120 --> 00:40:50,040
Easy.

635
00:40:52,440 --> 00:40:57,240
I hope you'll be a new man
in 32 hours, okay?

636
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:59,000
How about this?

637
00:40:59,080 --> 00:41:00,400
Let's take a photo

638
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:02,760
and post it on Moments.
Only they can see it.

639
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:03,920
Piss them off.

640
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:05,080
Get in the car.

641
00:41:05,160 --> 00:41:07,200
Just one photo.

642
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:08,440
I'm closing the door.

643
00:41:09,440 --> 00:41:10,640
I'm leaving.

644
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:12,640
Bye!

645
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:26,640
<i>Approved. Effective immediately,</i>

646
00:41:26,720 --> 00:41:29,880
<i>Xu Chi is transferred to the actuarial</i>
<i>team for the Celestial project.</i>

647
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:31,200
MA KE

648
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:33,000
<i>Back then,</i>

649
00:41:33,080 --> 00:41:35,560
<i>I suddenly remembered Su Su's WeChat bio.</i>

650
00:41:36,080 --> 00:41:39,720
<i>"Love comes and goes,</i>
<i>but work is forever."</i>

651
00:41:40,840 --> 00:41:45,080
<i>Tomorrow is always a new day.</i>

652
00:41:58,640 --> 00:42:01,520
I need a performance measurement tool
for the Actuarial Department.

653
00:42:01,600 --> 00:42:02,520
Do you have one?

654
00:42:04,320 --> 00:42:07,520
Balanced Scorecard or KSF-based
total performance compensation?

655
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:10,080
I've seen Lian'an Insurance's
in our files. Hold on.

656
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:15,120
Lian'an uses BSC. I'll send it to you.

657
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:19,000
I need the big data utilization rate
for Celestial's Actuarial Department.

658
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:20,440
17.3%.

659
00:42:21,240 --> 00:42:23,000
You can check data table two.

660
00:42:23,080 --> 00:42:24,680
- It has more details.
- Okay.

661
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:30,280
By the way, we have a video meeting
with external insurance data experts

662
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:31,680
tomorrow at ten.

663
00:42:31,760 --> 00:42:34,840
Ma Ke said anyone who wants
to ask questions live is welcome to join.

664
00:42:34,920 --> 00:42:35,600
Are you guys going?

665
00:42:35,680 --> 00:42:36,640
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

666
00:42:57,240 --> 00:42:58,760
Oh my God.

667
00:42:58,840 --> 00:43:01,200
It's only eight in the morning
and there's already such a long line.

668
00:43:01,280 --> 00:43:03,920
This is the limited-edition black truffle
milk tea that's going viral right now.

669
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:05,080
They only sell 200 cups a day.

670
00:43:05,160 --> 00:43:07,480
I heard every girl loves it.

671
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:09,320
- Let's go line up. Go.
- Let's go.

672
00:43:14,680 --> 00:43:15,600
Which flavor are you getting?

673
00:43:15,680 --> 00:43:17,720
Black truffle, of course.

674
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:19,120
That's what everyone's here for.

675
00:43:36,760 --> 00:43:37,920
Zhao Heng?

676
00:43:48,240 --> 00:43:49,400
You're not lining up?

677
00:43:49,480 --> 00:43:50,720
Someone bought it for me.

678
00:43:50,800 --> 00:43:51,880
Lucky you.

679
00:43:53,680 --> 00:43:54,920
Can you save me a spot?

680
00:44:02,840 --> 00:44:03,880
Take it.

681
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:06,360
I don't like milk tea.

682
00:44:09,760 --> 00:44:12,440
Didn't you say
you'd never talk to me again?

683
00:44:13,040 --> 00:44:13,960
Then why did you…?
